  "details": "### Description\n\nIn Open Beta build 1912, after joining a world, the first attempt to change my avatar to one of my own uploaded avatars always displays the following message:\n\n> “This user has cloning turned off.”\n\nThis happens even though I am trying to select my own uploaded avatar, not clone another user's avatar.\n\nClicking the avatar a second time allows the avatar change to complete normally.\n\nI have also seen this message appear in other situations, but I have not yet identified reliable reproduction steps for those cases.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Launch VRChat using Open Beta build 1912 in Desktop mode.\n\n2. Join a world.\n\n3. Open the avatar menu.\n\n4. Select one of your own uploaded avatars as the first avatar change after joining the world.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\n“This user has cloning turned off.” is displayed, and the avatar does not change on the first click.\n\nClicking the same avatar a second time successfully changes to it.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nSelecting one of my own uploaded avatars should change the avatar immediately without displaying a cloning-related error message.\n\n### Frequency\n\nEvery time.\n\n### Environment\n\nDesktop mode\n\nOpen Beta build 1912",
